topics.detail:
Musk Donations argues that Musk's massive donations are obscene and big money should be banned. Musk's donations are an attempt to buy political influence. Musk's spending on the midterms is excessive and undermines democracy. Musk Citizenship argues that Musk's citizenship is not a popularity contest. Musk's citizenship should be investigated for fraud. Musk's immigration paperwork should be investigated.

@deanobeidallah.bsky.social: “NEW AND UNREAL: Inside Elon Musk’s $276 Million Midterm Rescue Mission for Republicans. Musk has donated a massive amount of $. This is obscene. Big $ must be banned in politics!”

Musk Donations (73.1%) says Musk donates heavily to Republicans. Musk Citizenship (26.9%) says Musk's citizenship is questioned.

Trans Rights argues that Trans people are dehumanized and face transphobia. Trans people are denied basic humanity and rights. Trans people are harassed and face bigotry. Trans people are made responsible for others' actions. Trans people face transphobic nonsense and discrimination. Dems Fail Trans argues that Dems lean into transphobia to lose. Dem states lack trans healthcare access. Dems are better than Republicans on trans issues.

@antonarcana.gay: “For as much as I (as a trans person myself) understand that dysphoria is genuinely life ruining when it comes to your own body, I think it’s weird and shitty to police how other trans people draw ourselves.”

Trans Rights (93.4%) says Trans people face discrimination and transphobia. Dems Fail Trans (6.6%) says Dems fail to support trans issues.

Data Centers argues that Data centers drive global fascism. Data centers commoditize cloud resources. Data centers spread disinformation. Data centers harm local communities. Data centers threaten energy supply. Data centers should be targeted. Data Center Critics argues that Some posts argue that data centers have negative consequences, such as reinforcing a police surveillance state or causing environmental problems.

@chrononaut.bsky.social: “The "AI data center construction boom" label obfuscates a huge push to commoditize cloud resources. Tech companies don't want you to run or store anything locally. They want you to only own a terminal and pay them license fees for using their resources and software.”

Data Centers (92.9%) says Data centers are problematic. Data Center Critics (7.1%) says Some posts argue that data centers have negative consequences, such as reinforcing a police surveillance state or causing environmental problems.

World.detail:
