Oil Price Impact (83.9%) says Trump's actions won't lower oil prices. Diesel Price (16.1%) says Ukraine affects diesel prices.

Corporate Ethics argues that Corporations prioritize profits over customers. Starbucks Not Buying argues that Starbucks spokesperson denies plans to buy Chipotle.

@dominiconline.bsky.social: “Starbucks CANNOT buy Chipotle before the recognize a union contract…I’m doing well boycotting Starbucks, but boycotting Chipotle would be genuinely detrimental to my health (I have a rare condition and the only cure is burritos)”

Corporate Ethics (75%) says Corporations prioritize profits over customers. Starbucks Not Buying (25%) says Starbucks spokesperson denies plans to buy Chipotle.

Robot Labor argues that Robots can replace teams of people with one human manager. Robots are used to automate supply-chain sites. Robots are like slaves with no wages. Job Replacement argues that Employers replace experienced workers with new hires.

@chimerror.blacksky.app: “On the last point, I'm sure there are some people who think robots are ready to completely replace human labor, but more likely they know that they can replace a whole team of people with a bunch of robots and a human wrangler.”

Robot Labor (50%) says Robots replace human labor. Job Replacement (50%) says Employers replace experienced workers with new hires.

Diesel Price argues that High diesel prices cut truck routes. Exports cause diesel price spikes. Russia benefits from diesel exports. Dyed Diesel Concerns argues that Many are warning against using dyed diesel fuel due to potential damage to trucks and fines for contamination.

@isaiahbishop.bsky.social: “Theyre doing this for like 3 days of of US diesel exports every month”

Diesel Price (54.5%) says Diesel prices are high due to exports. Dyed Diesel Concerns (45.5%) says Many are warning against using dyed diesel fuel due to potential damage to trucks and fines for contamination.

Housing Market argues that borrowing to invest in old houses to claim tax losses. Sellers becoming distressed due to over-leveraging. Removing stamp duty will not bring down house prices. Tax Abolition argues that Most posts argue against abolishing house tax, citing its potential to exacerbate existing issues like class warfare and skyrocketing house prices.

