Health.detail:
Pneumonic Plague argues that Pneumonic plague requires close contact and is treatable with antibiotics. Pneumonic plague is more treatable and less transmissible than COVID19. Russia's handling of the plague situation could be a learning experience for other militaries. Unverified plague treatments are being promoted online due to an unconfirmed death in Russia. The World Health Organization has reported a pneumonic plague discovery in Russia. Covid Risk argues that Covid is still killing people. Covid is nothing to worry about. Covid is on the rise again.

@cvmedia.bsky.social: “Russia is investigating a lab worker’s death after unconfirmed reports of pneumonic plague. Experts say it requires close contact, is treatable with antibiotics and poses little risk of widespread transmission. #Russia #PublicHealth”

Pneumonic Plague (58.3%) says Pneumonic plague poses little risk of widespread transmission. Covid Risk (41.7%) says Covid is still a threat.

Health Care argues that Consistent support is vital to keep people safe and healthy. Long-term health effects are being ignored. Investing in public health is necessary. Protein Fad argues that Added protein may not be necessary.

@midnight0wl.bsky.social: “our action matters. consistent visibility & support are vital to keep people safe. don't let them be forced to choose between medical care or proper food for their family. we have the ability to create change. step up & choose to be a lifeline. people are worth every effort. 💸💕”

Health Care (66.7%) says People need access to medical care. Protein Fad (33.3%) says Added protein may not be necessary.

Clinic Legitimacy argues that Clinic is legitimate. Raw Milk Danger argues that Raw milk can give young children listeria and bird flu. Pediatricians recommend avoiding raw milk for young children's safety. Raw milk consumption is a health risk for kids due to potential bacterial and viral contamination.

@cphickie.bsky.social: “I listened to CHD-TV's show yesterday interviewing the parents who presented their children at the ceremony opening this "clinic". They are stated they got last-minute invites with no information as to what was happening or what to say.”

Clinic Legitimacy (71.4%) says Clinic is legitimate. Raw Milk Danger (28.6%) says Raw milk poses health risks to young children.

Disease Control argues that Disease control measures are crucial. Cancer Trends argues that Cancer rates are rising faster in younger people. HPV immunisation has reduced cervical cancers. Cancer survival rates have substantially increased.

@dsky.bsky.social: “Yeah exactly. Like, when a disease is common, there is a lot more reward to control measures. As you move closer to extinction (think polio, smallpox, etc) it costs more per case to do the work to prevent the next breakthrough. But you MUST do that last 20 years to really end it.”

Disease Control (62.5%) says Disease control measures are crucial. Cancer Trends (37.5%) says Cancer rates and outcomes are changing.

Drug Testing argues that testing drugs ensures safer choices and bodily autonomy. Lack of data on adverse effects hinders understanding of drug harm. Drug efficacy is not properly proven without testing. Harm Reduction argues that Drugs can help with mental health disorders.

@britculpsapp.bsky.social: “anyways, this is a big reason i highly encourage everyone who uses drugs at any amount & frequency these days to test their drugs; beyond safety, its a bodily autonomy & consent issue we also often make safer choices for ourselves when we have the information to do so”

Drug Testing (60%) says Drug testing is important for safety and autonomy. Harm Reduction (40%) says Drugs can help with mental health disorders.

Environment.detail:
